<title>FINLAND: FINNISH SEPT TIMBER CUTTINGS DOWN 10 PCT - METLA.</title>
<headline>FINNISH SEPT TIMBER CUTTINGS DOWN 10 PCT - METLA.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1996-11-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Raw timber market cuttings fell 10 percent year-on-year in September to 3.73 million cubic metres, the Finnish Forest Research Institute (METLA) said in a monthly review on Wednesday.</p>
<p>But raw timber cuttings in September were 18 percent higher than September cuttings during the last ten years on average, it said.</p>
<p>METLA said timber cuttings in January-September fell 14 percent year-on-year to 31.7 million cubic metres.</p>
<p>-- Helsinki newsroom +358-0-6805 0248</p>
</text>
